#. type: 標題
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:1
msgid "# Benefits of Open Source"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:3
msgid ""
"Open Source Software (OSS) is indispensable in modern software development.\n"
"Much of the [primary technology used (e.g., cloud platforms, mobile UI frameworks, data analytics platforms)] used daily in [Company Name] operations relies on OSS.\n"
"These OSS projects represent collective wisdom and experience brought together by developers worldwide to solve common problems.\n"
"Understanding and leveraging OSS appropriately is becoming a vital skill for developers and management alike."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:4
msgid "This document details representative benefits gained from utilizing OSS from both developer and management perspectives."
msgstr ""

#. type: 標題
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:5
msgid "## Benefits for Developers"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:6
msgid "Leveraging OSS offers developers numerous advantages. Key highlights include:"
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:7
msgid "1. **Avoiding Reinventing the Wheel and Focusing on High-Value Engineering**"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:8
msgid ""
"    When building new services or capabilities, developers do not need to construct everything from scratch.\n"
"    For instance, [examples of internally used OSS (e.g., web frameworks, database connector libraries)] used daily at [Company Name] represent OSS continuously refined over years by global developers, proving their reliability and performance."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:9
msgid ""
"    Building such components in-house from scratch would overwhelm teams with security patching, performance tuning, and bug fixing—diverting resources away from delivering core customer value and product differentiators.\n"
"    That would be equivalent to reinventing the wheel from scratch."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:10
msgid "    Smart OSS utilization represents a strategy for concentrating limited time on high-value engineering."
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:11
msgid "2. **Leveraging High-Quality Code and Global Domain Expertise**"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:12
msgid ""
"    OSS code undergoes continuous refinement under widespread public inspection.\n"
"    Bugs overlooked in closed development processes are discovered and resolved quickly through global user feedback and contributions."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:13
msgid ""
"    For example, in [Major OSS Project Name] used at [Company Name], daily Pull Requests and Issues drive continuous security remediation and performance optimization.\n"
"    Developers build upon these trusted foundations to deliver new value with confidence."
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:14
msgid "3. **Mastering Modern Engineering Practices and Cutting-Edge Technologies**"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:15
msgid ""
"    Most OSS projects run transparently on GitHub, naturally incorporating modern practices like CI/CD pipelines, automated testing, and code reviews.\n"
"    Engaging with these projects gives developers hands-on experience with industry best practices that are difficult to master solely within internal environments."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:16
msgid "    In key domains like [focused technology area (e.g., cloud-native, microservices)], OSS projects lead technology trends, making active participation a direct path to skill development."
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:17
msgid "4. **Problem-Solving Speed and Flexibility**"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:18
msgid ""
"    In proprietary software, bug fixes and feature releases depend entirely on vendor roadmaps.\n"
"    In contrast, because OSS source code is accessible, teams can apply patches directly and adapt software to internal requirements rapidly.\n"
"    This flexibility provides a significant advantage during urgent security fixes or custom feature integrations."
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:19
msgid "5. **Growth Through Community Collaboration**"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:20
msgid ""
"    Contributing to open source gives developers opportunities to collaborate with leading engineers worldwide.\n"
"    Submitting bug reports or proposing fixes exposes developers to diverse ideas and solutions beyond single-organization viewpoints.\n"
"    Furthermore, contributing modifications upstream ensures continuous benefit from subsequent improvements made by other global developers."
msgstr ""

#. type: 標題
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:21
msgid "## Benefits for Management"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:22
msgid "Strategic OSS adoption offers management substantial strategic advantages:"
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:23
msgid "1. **Cost Optimization and Efficient Capital Allocation**"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:24
msgid "    Adopting open source transforms enterprise cost structures—shifting spend from recurring license fees toward targeted investments in customization and implementation."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:25
msgid ""
"    Training, maintenance, and support costs exist in both open source and proprietary software.\n"
"    With proprietary software, licensing fees add an extra cost layer that obscures total cost visibility.\n"
"    With open source, because software usage itself carries no licensing fees, cost breakdowns become transparent."
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:26
msgid "2. **Enhanced Talent Development**"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:27
msgid ""
"    Open source participation provides developers with ideal learning environments.\n"
"    Encouraging employee participation in open source projects develops technical capabilities alongside soft skills, including communication, project management, and teamwork."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:28
msgid "    Collaborating with global engineers exposes employees to new technologies and methodologies, broadening technical perspectives beyond traditional internal training capabilities."
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:29
msgid "3. **Risk Diversification and Long-Term Operational Stability**"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:30
msgid ""
"    Proprietary software carries vendor lock-in risks—such as abrupt product deprecation or support termination driven by vendor business shifts or bankruptcy.\n"
"    With open source, accessible source code allows internal teams to maintain software or identify alternative maintainers as needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:31
msgid "    Because open source communities operate independently of single-vendor profit motives, sustaining long-term software improvements is simpler, providing vital operational stability for enterprise longevity."
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:32
msgid "4. **Recruiting Advantage and Technical Brand Enhancement**"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:33
msgid "    Recruiting top engineering talent is a continuous priority for enterprises. Active participation in open source projects serves as an effective showcase of corporate technical strength. Prospective engineers gain clear visibility into the organization's technical challenges and engineering culture through public code repositories and workflows."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:34
msgid "    Furthermore, maintainers of successful open source projects gain industry recognition, directly enhancing the corporate brand value of their employer."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:38
msgid "**Mandatory Items**"
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:39
msgid ""
"- [ ] Replaced all instances of [Company Name] with actual company name.\n"
"- [ ] Replaced placeholders like [primary technology used] and [Major OSS Project Name] with concrete information.\n"
"- [ ] Stated the connection between corporate mission/vision/strategy and OSS activities in the introduction."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:40
msgid "**Developer Section**"
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:41
msgid ""
"- [ ] Listed specific OSS projects used daily by internal development teams.\n"
"- [ ] Adjusted benefit ordering based on industry characteristics.\n"
"- [ ] Incorporated internal success stories."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:42
msgid "**Management Section**"
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:43
msgid ""
"- [ ] Provided concrete metrics or track records illustrating cost structure transformation.\n"
"- [ ] Explicitly linked talent development strategy with OSS activities.\n"
"- [ ] Calibrated tone for target reader roles (Executives / Middle Managers / Project Managers)."
msgstr ""

#. type: 註解
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:44
msgid ""
