#. type: 標題
#: operation-templates/about/opensource-guide.md:1
msgid "# [Company Name] Open Source Guide"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/opensource-guide.md:3
msgid ""
"This document was created to promote the strategic adoption of open source software at [Company Name] and ensure appropriate, effective utilization.\n"
"In modern software engineering, open source is not merely an option—it forms the core foundation for innovation and business growth."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/opensource-guide.md:4
msgid ""
"Open source software delivers immense corporate benefits, including accelerated development velocity, transformed cost structures, faster technology innovation, employee professional growth, and top talent acquisition.\n"
"However, usage entails critical considerations: license compliance, preventing IP contamination, handling software defects, and mitigating security vulnerabilities.\n"
"Through robust compliance management and open source community engagement, organizations effectively control these risks while maximizing open source value."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/opensource-guide.md:5
msgid ""
"This guide systematically organizes open source topics—from foundational concepts to practical workflows.\n"
"It provides actionable guidance for developers, product managers, technical leaders, and stakeholders across open source workflows."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/opensource-guide.md:6
msgid "If you have questions, refer to \"[What Is an OSPO?](../about/ospo.md)\" to contact responsible OSPO staff."
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/opensource-guide.md:10
msgid ""
"- [ ] Replaced all instances of [Company Name] with actual company name.\n"
"- [ ] Documented strategic rationales for engaging with open source in the introduction.\n"
"- [ ] Established feedback channels (for improvement suggestions and inquiries).\n"
"- [ ] Verified consistency with subsequent sections (About Open Source, Compliance, etc.)."
msgstr ""

