#. type: 標題
#: operation-templates/about/ospo.md:1
msgid "# What Is an OSPO?"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/ospo.md:3
msgid "An Open Source Program Office (OSPO) is an organizational framework designed to drive the strategic utilization of and healthy contribution to open source software (OSS). Organizational structures and focus areas vary across enterprises; at [Company Name], the OSPO functions as **[Company OSPO Positioning and Priority Areas]**."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/ospo.md:4
msgid "The primary role of the OSPO is establishing **policy formulation**, **guideline maintenance**, and **governance frameworks** for internal open source activities, overseeing:"
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/ospo.md:5
msgid ""
"- Formulating open source usage policies and license guidelines\n"
"- Establishing compliance management frameworks in coordination with stakeholder departments\n"
"- Facilitating engagement with internal and external open source communities\n"
"- Monitoring technology trends and providing strategic recommendations to executive management\n"
"- Building mechanisms empowering employee contributions to OSS\n"
"- [Company-Specific OSPO Initiatives]"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/ospo.md:6
msgid "At [Company Name], the OSPO operates as a **[Operating Model (e.g., Virtual Team (V-Team) Model)]** led by **[Lead Department Name]**, bringing together members from **[Partner Dept 1 (e.g., Legal)]**, **[Partner Dept 2 (e.g., Security)]**, and **[Partner Dept 3 (e.g., Engineering)]**."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/ospo.md:7
msgid ""
"The OSPO is **not a helpdesk performing OSS operational tasks on behalf of teams**; rather, it designs policies, rules, and workflows that empower the entire organization to manage OSS autonomously.\n"
"(Hence the title **\"Open Source Program Office\"** rather than \"Open Source Support Office.\")"
msgstr ""

